WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.799
Most agencies run ScubaGear,
save the HTML report,

2
00:00:03.799 --> 00:00:06.450
and reopen it when an assessor asks.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.623
The program instead treats each tool as an
adapter, one input to one evidence chain,

4
00:00:11.623 --> 00:00:15.350
and leaves the tools exactly
as their publishers ship them.

5
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.763
Each run flows through four stages.

6
00:00:17.763 --> 00:00:20.562
The tool writes its own unaltered output.

7
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:24.012
Each result becomes a claim
in a provenance envelope:

8
00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:27.462
who issued it, when it was
extracted, and a lineage hash.

9
00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:31.112
Claims from one interval are
assembled into a sealed bundle.

10
00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:34.024
And the bundle emits
OSCAL assessment results

11
00:00:34.024 --> 00:00:36.488
and plan of action and milestones items.

12
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:44.799
Take MS.AAD.1.1v1, legacy authentication
shall be blocked, which CISA maps to CM-7.

13
00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:45.950
Say it fails.

14
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.185
The claim's lineage hash
ties it to the raw result,

15
00:00:49.185 --> 00:00:51.288
and the bundle opens a POA&M item.

16
00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:55.065
Months later an assessor can
rebuild the bundle, check its hash,

17
00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:58.551
and walk back to the raw output
without re-running the tool.

18
00:00:58.551 --> 00:00:59.875
The limits are stated.

19
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:03.200
ScubaGear runs on an
interval, not continuously.

20
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.900
And there's no ScubaGoggles adapter
yet, so Google Workspace is a gap.
